---
interface Props{kind:'signals'|'lora'|'preferences'}
const {kind}=Astro.props,id='tuning-'+kind;
const titles={signals:'Demonstrations teach a target. Preferences compare targets.',lora:'Keep the base path. Learn a smaller update path.',preferences:'Two ways to learn from the same preference pairs.'};
const captions={signals:'Figure 1. SFT trains on a desired completion for a prompt. Preference learning compares two completions under the same prompt and rubric. Both change behavior through optimization; neither makes an unsupported label true.',lora:'Figure 2. For column-vector input x, a frozen base computes W₀x. Trainable A compresses to rank r, B projects back, and α/r scales the update before addition. The adapter contributes to the output without updating W₀.',preferences:'Figure 3. A common RLHF recipe learns a reward model, then optimizes a policy using sampled responses and reference-based regularization. Standard offline DPO instead trains the policy directly on fixed preferred/rejected pairs with a fixed reference. Both need independent evaluation.'};
const pairs=kind==='signals'?[['SFT input','Prompt + movie card'],['SFT target','One desired answer'],['Preference input','Same prompt + card'],['Preference label','Chosen vs rejected']]:[['Preference pairs','Same prompt + rubric'],['Reward model','Predict relative quality'],['RL policy updates','Sample, score, constrain'],['Direct policy updates','DPO pair loss + reference']];
---
<figure class="diagram"><div class="figure-title"><span class="figure-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>{titles[kind]}</div><div class="diagram-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={titles[kind]}><svg viewBox="0 0 760 290" role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-title ${id}-desc`}><title id={`${id}-title`}>{titles[kind]}</title><desc id={`${id}-desc`}>{captions[kind]}</desc><defs><marker id={`${id}-arrow`} markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8Z" fill="var(--accent)"/></marker></defs>
{kind==='signals'&&<>{pairs.map(([title,sub],i)=>{const x=i%2?426:24,y=i<2?24:166;return <g><rect x={x} y={y} width="308" height="84" rx="8" fill={i%2?'var(--accent-soft)':'var(--panel)'} stroke="var(--line)"/><text x={x+154} y={y+32} text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="18">{title}</text><text x={x+154} y={y+60} text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="15">{sub}</text></g>})}<path d="M344 66 H412" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><path d="M344 208 H412" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><text x="380" y="139" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">A demonstration is an example. A preference is a comparison.</text></>}
{kind==='lora'&&<><rect x="20" y="98" width="90" height="64" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="65" y="136" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="18">Input x</text><path d="M120 130 H145 V58 H292 M145 130 V222 H184" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="300" y="23" width="206" height="70" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="403" y="53" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="18">Frozen W₀</text><text x="403" y="78" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">d-out × d-in</text><path d="M516 58 H598 V114" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/>{[['A','r × d-in',194],['B','d-out × r',334],['α / r','scale',474]].map(([t,sub,x])=><g><rect x={x} y="186" width="114" height="70" rx="8" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x={Number(x)+57} y="216" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="18">{t}</text><text x={Number(x)+57} y="241" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">{sub}</text></g>)}<path d="M314 222 H326" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><path d="M454 222 H466" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><path d="M594 222 H598 V151" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><circle cx="598" cy="133" r="16" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)"/><text x="598" y="139" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="22">+</text><path d="M622 133 H656" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><text x="701" y="139" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="16">Output</text><text x="380" y="281" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">Only A and B are trained in this illustrated layer.</text></>}
{kind==='preferences'&&<><rect x="20" y="97" width="194" height="90" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="117" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="17">Preference pairs</text><text x="117" y="157" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">Same prompt + rubric</text><path d="M224 142 H248 V61 H272" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><path d="M248 142 V223 H272" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><rect x="286" y="20" width="174" height="82" rx="8" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="373" y="54" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="17">Reward model</text><text x="373" y="79" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">Learn a scorer</text><path d="M470 61 H520" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}/><rect x="534" y="20" width="206" height="82" rx="8" fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="637" y="54" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="17">RL policy updates</text><text x="637" y="79" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">Score sampled replies</text><rect x="286" y="182" width="454" height="82" rx="8" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="513" y="216" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-size="17">DPO: direct policy updates on fixed pairs</text><text x="513" y="241" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">Compare policy log-ratios with a fixed reference</text><text x="510" y="143" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="14">Evaluate useful behavior separately from training loss.</text></>}
</svg></div><figcaption>{captions[kind]}</figcaption></figure>
